<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani rupee ends low in kerb, seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistani rupee ends low in kerb, seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistani rupee ended 0.03 lower in the kerb market at 40.31 to the dollar on Wednesday as dollar demand rose after the U.S. currency strengthened abroad, dealers said.</p>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan rate, last changed on September 10, was 36.9700/37.1549 to the dollar.</p>
<p>The premium on the foreign exchange bearer certificates closed unchanged at 8.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
